    {
      "id": "ff10p10.q.ext2",
      "type": "case_based",
      "marks": 5,
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "concepts": [
        "true_love"
      ],
      "source": {
        "kind": "shine"
      },
      "question": "Read the extract and answer the questions.\n\n*That only God, my dear,*\n*Could love you for yourself alone*\n*And not your yellow hair.*\n\n(i) Who had said that only God could love her for herself?\n\n(ii) What does 'for yourself alone' mean?\n\n(iii) What do people usually love her for?\n\n(iv) What is the theme of these lines?\n\n(v) Name the poet.",
      "status": "reviewed",
      "answer_steps": [
        "(i) An old religious man.",
        "(ii) For her inner qualities, her real self.",
        "(iii) Her yellow hair, her outward beauty.",
        "(iv) True love sees inner beauty; only God loves that way.",
        "(v) W. B. Yeats."
      ],
      "marking_scheme": [
        "(i) 1 mark",
        "(ii) 1 mark",
        "(iii) 1 mark",
        "(iv) 1 mark",
        "(v) 1 mark"
      ]
    },
